        "id": 1305927
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-02-02T17:01:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Which CL are you referring to? I mostly see code movement without API changes, but I haven\u0027t dug in yet.\n\nI was envisioning something like the Zephyr link that Keith provided, where the header file provides `inline`, empty implementations of the functions in the case where the relevant config is disabled. Then it\u0027s the DP library (header file) that is responsible for doing something reasonable in the case where the config is disabled, not the user of the library. From the DPM\u0027s POV, it would just be as if DP never does anything.",
      "parentUuid": "98a96f68_27f95a8f",
      "revId": "8d5c8458cb7e73379b533da4e02e4dabf4773568",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
