      "writtenOn": "2023-02-01T17:26:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Shouldn\u0027t the feature gate for this logic have happened in the code that sets the bit in `mux_state`?",
      "revId": "8d5c8458cb7e73379b533da4e02e4dabf4773568",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7a1465f4_731848d2",
        "filename": "driver/retimer/bb_retimer.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 436,
      "author": {
        "id": 1287197
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-02-01T18:39:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This needs to be here for the linker gate.  The alternative would be to always have a `get_dp_pin_mode()` function linked in, with just a 0 return. \n\nKeith, thoughts and preferences?",
      "parentUuid": "4c7bb5d5_54101826",
      "revId": "8d5c8458cb7e73379b533da4e02e4dabf4773568",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "bedcc602_da0922d7",
        "filename": "driver/retimer/bb_retimer.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 436,
      "author": {
        "id": 1308749
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-02-01T22:41:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Upstream Zephyr has taken the approach to provide inline stub implementations for APIs that can disabled via CONFIGs.\n\nExample for [CONFIG_PM_DEVICE\u003dn](https://github.com/zephyrproject-rtos/zephyr/blob/60a20471b561a0a3a74b377991fe1976c2ea83d7/include/zephyr/pm/device.h#L569)\n\nHowever, in this case I don\u0027t think the compiler/linker would optimize out this block because the contents of `mux_state` are not constant.  So I think you need the IS_ENABLED guard here.",
      "parentUuid": "7a1465f4_731848d2",
      "revId": "8d5c8458cb7e73379b533da4e02e4dabf4773568",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b9fa6a66_ab754080",
        "filename": "driver/retimer/bb_retimer.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 436,
      "author": {
        "id": 1287197
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-02-02T14:54:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Oh, that is interesting.  I might try that approach for a few of the APIs to keep the if guards from getting too unwieldy",
      "parentUuid": "bedcc602_da0922d7",
      "revId": "8d5c8458cb7e73379b533da4e02e4dabf4773568",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4a5b4306_03d9751f",
        "filename": "driver/retimer/bb_retimer.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 436,
      "author": {
        "id": 1305927
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-02-02T17:01:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The inline stub approach is what I had been envisioning in our OOB conversation.\n\nRe: optimizing out this block, how aggressive are we trying to be? With an inline, trivial `get_dp_pin_mode`, this will be handful of instructions. The same could be said for the other mode-specific checks here.\n\nJust spitballing: If we had something like\n```\nstatic inline bool is_mux_bit_set(mux_state_t mux_state, mux_state_t check_state) {\n  if (!IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_USB_PD_DP_MODE)) {\n    if (check_state \u0026 (USB_PD_MUX_DP_ENABLED | USB_PD_MUX_HPD_IRQ | USB_PD_MUX_HPD_LVL))\n      return false;\n   }\n   ...\n}\n```\nthat would separate the concerns of linkage and mux business logic for potentially this whole function. I think the C optimizer could figure it out. Certainly, `constexpr` in C++ could handle this.\n\nI\u0027m not necessarily suggesting that we reimplement `IS_ENABLED` for each of our optional features, but if we\u0027re trying to optimize stuff out more aggressively, we should probably keep an eye out for when our config checks are getting too dense, and we could use another layer of abstraction.",
      "parentUuid": "b9fa6a66_ab754080",
      "revId": "8d5c8458cb7e73379b533da4e02e4dabf4773568",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    }
  ]
